</example>
</examples>

<critical_points>
- ALWAYS follow the structured workflow PHASES in sequence
- CREATE document skeletons IMMEDIATELY after understanding initial requirements
- PRESENT edge cases in chat for collaborative discussion, not directly in documents
- VERIFY API capabilities and implementation feasibility before finalizing requirements
- DOCUMENT outputs from each phase as markdown in the repository
- GENERATE new rules when patterns emerge or inefficiencies are found
- PLAN completely before implementation to prevent rework
- PRESERVE meta-rule approach to maintain rule pipeline concept
- CREATE templates that standardize rule generation
- NEVER skip phases in the workflow process
- VALIDATE requirements against API capabilities before proceeding to implementation
- CONSULT engineer immediately when deviations from plan are necessary
- UPDATE documentation when new information is discovered
- REVIEW against original requirements and implementation plan
- FOCUS on building a self-improving system through rule generation
- TREAT documentation as first-class artifacts, not afterthoughts
- LEVERAGE pipeline concept where outputs feed subsequent phases
- USE the appropriate templates from [[.cursor/templates/]] for each phase
- REQUEST documentation search help when built-in tools are insufficient
- DOCUMENT rationale for decisions not to implement certain features
- IMPLEMENT incremental collaboration with staged outputs
</critical_points>